{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I create.</b> All the commentators said that the Name is the one who creates, and the word 'said' is missing — had it not been unfitting to innovate, I would have said that it is the language of creation, from the root of 'creating darkness' (Isaiah 45:7)." "<b>And the word 'fruit' is like 'produce.'</b> As in 'the produce of Shaddai' (Deuteronomy 32:13). And the meaning is speech, and likewise its interpretation is 'I said peace to the far and the near' — He announced that He has already healed Israel, and the meaning is 'and I will heal him.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {1 "Resolved the elided referent of והטעם 'its interpretation' as referring back to the verse's meaning; the final ורפאתיו echoes the same root from the preceding verse (Isaiah 57:19/57:18)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:03.123739773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}